# ── Rust build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
sample
# Keep Cargo.lock tracked (Orchester ships binaries).
.cargo
# ── Forschung: cloned reference repos ───────────────────────────────
# 50+ upstream repos live here purely as read-only reference. Never commit
# them (each carries its own .git). Keep only our own analysis + notes.
/forschung/*
!/forschung/ANALYSIS.md
!/forschung/README.md
# Legacy name before the German rename (belt & braces):
/agent-research/
/forschung/.analysis_parts/

# ── Frontend build output ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The JavaScript workspace starts at the repository root. Its lockfile IS
# tracked (the Pages and desktop builds run --frozen-lockfile), everything
# derived is not.
node_modules/
/.pnpm-store/
apps/*/dist/
# The Pages site is nested deeper than the surface glob.
apps/web/site/dist/
apps/web/site/dist-*/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
# apps/web builds straight into the server crate that serves it.
/kisten/netz/static/
# Tauri generates these next to src-tauri; the config beside them is tracked.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# ── Local runtime / tooling state ───────────────────────────────────
.remember/logs/
.remember/tmp/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
tmp/
# Session scratch: extraction scripts, fetched pages and intermediate reports.
# Never part of a commit; the durable conclusions live in docs/design.
/_scratch/
# The governed process runtime calls env_clear() before spawning a tool, so a
# powershell.exe child loses LOCALAPPDATA and writes its module cache relative
# to the test's working directory instead of the user profile.
**/Microsoft/Windows/PowerShell/
prompt
# ── Editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
docs/local
/docs/superpowers/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.txt
*.md
!/README.md
!/docs/README.zh-TW.md
!/docs/README.en.md
!/npm/cli/README.md
!/docs/PLAN-FRONTENDS.md
!/apps/README.md
# The Codex-informed UI design record is a tracked deliverable. The blanket
# *.md rule above exists to keep session notes out, so these need to opt back
# in explicitly — the directory first, then the files inside it.
!/docs/design/
!/docs/design/*.md
# The release procedure is the same kind of thing: it describes how this
# repository publishes, and it is worthless if it only exists on one machine.
!/docs/RELEASE-PROCEDURE.md
.playwright-mcp/
.superpowers/
.worktrees/
